{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he believed in HaShem, and He counted it to him as righteousness.</b> The explanation follows the way of our Sages of blessed memory (Rosh HaShanah 6a), that the law of righteousness is like vows — for one who vows to the Most High is as one who delivers to a private person. And that is what the verse says: <b>וְהֶאֱמִין בַַה׳</b> — meaning, he deposited the blessing with Him. And if you would say: but it had not yet come to his hand to deposit it in the hand of a trustee — therefore it says <b>וַיַּחְשְׁבֶהָ לּוֹ צְדָקָה</b>, meaning, Abraham accounted what HaShem said to him as righteousness, and since this is so, it has the legal status of delivery, and he trusted it in the hand of HaShem." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend that He promised him — namely, that his children would be righteous. And this matter is not in the hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, as they said of blessed memory (Berakhot 33b): all is in the hand of Heaven except for the fear of Heaven. The verse says that he believed in HaShem that He would do so, and he did not harbor thoughts against His attributes to say 'but surely…' etc., and HaShem counted it to Abraham as righteousness for having gone beyond the limit on behalf of the righteous. Or it may allude in this vein to the fact that even though from HaShem's side it was intended that there be thirty righteous in the world (Genesis Rabbah, chapter 35 and chapter 49) — if so, He desires to incline a person toward the straight path, and this man has no legal claim of righteousness such as the verse states (Deuteronomy 6:25): ״וּצְדָקָה תִּהְיֶה לָּנוּ כִּי נִשְׁמֹר״ etc. From that point on, the thirty righteous are under compulsion in their deeds. Therefore it says that even so, <b>וַיַּחְשְׁבֶהָ ה׳ לוֹ צְדָקָה</b> — meaning, to the seed mentioned in the immediate context, for it is written ״יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ,״ since there is an allusion to the thirty in the numerical value of 'יִהְיֶה.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:27.533524384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}